HE-AAC v1 follow-ups:
- shared signal detector ("share the detector, not the filter"): one analysis
  pass over the (full-rate, HF-bearing) input yielding transient position/strength
  and per-band tonality, consumed by every actuator that today rolls its own:
  core block-switch (blockswitch.c), SBR numEnvelopes + envelope border + noise
  floor + invf mode (sbr.c SBRAnalysis), and the TNS whitening gate. Run it on
  the full-rate signal in doHEAACPreprocess (already de-interleaved as fullPtrs).
- SBR noise floor / invf mode from tonality (now fixed 4 / 3). A first adaptive
  try (across-band spectral flatness of QMF band energies -> noise level) was
  net-NEGATIVE: broadband-bright clips read as "flat" and kept noise, peaky-noisy
  clips read as "tonal" and lost it. Needs a within-band/temporal tonality measure
  (or the proper original-vs-transposed-estimate ratio), not band-energy flatness.
- SBR envelope border at the transient (kills highband pre-echo): needs the
  variable frame classes VARFIX/FIXVAR/VARVAR + bs_rel_bord; today only FIXFIX
  (equal-spaced borders) is written, so 2-envelope frames just split at the midpoint.
- write_sbr_noise: use dedicated noise Huffman tables, not the envelope table
  (BLOCKED: numNoiseBands is hardcoded to 1, so the delta-coded nb>0 branch that
  would use a noise table never runs; this is a no-op until multi-noise-band
  coding lands -- see the shared-detector / tonality follow-ups above).
- validate MP4 container path: explicit-hierarchy ASC + full-rate samplerate
- simplify compute_kx/compute_k2 magic numbers (cite ISO 14496-3 tables)
- add SBR/resample sanity tests
